From f8a856c2b1fd47d1e34e517b1d34c023fde2693f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:21:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] drm/asahi: t6050: identify the M5 Pro's G17S firmware
 builds

The M5 Pro admits no firmware image (Firmware::Identified(&[])), so
even with bare-metal tables it could only refuse whatever the boot
loader left in fw-text.

Pin the G17S builds of both roles, measured the way fwid defines a
build (the SHA-256 of the primary's then the secondary's TEXT with the
entropy records, the two header load fields and the two boot-argument
sections of each role zeroed):

  27.3 beta 1 (26C5035r)  b5537c8f06bd...66763600
  27.2 (26B123)           2b4613c62a8a...913f0fd9
  27.0 (26A428)           85d0fd8280f7...b94739c6

The images are the a010 (FW Build variant: g17s) entries of
armfw_g17x.im4p and armfw1_g17x.im4p: the public Mac17,8 IPSWs for
27.0 and 27.2, and the 27.3 beta 1 restore bundle (im4p SHA-256
ae7f35b1... and da8ff3fb...). The offsets come from each image's
Mach-O load commands: TEXT 0x50000 + 0x54000, DATA 0x184000 as on the
M5 Max, the _rtk_tunables and _rtk_patchbay sections per role. 27.2
needs an entry of its own although its interface matches 27.3's: its
primary entropy record sits at 0x49ea4, 27.3's at 0x49eac. Each image
header still carries its load fields at 0x224/0x23c (zero in the file,
the patchbay's offset and size at 0x22c/0x230, as in 26A428).

The same digest tool reproduces Aurora's two pinned 26A428 digests,
G17C 304d8544...ecb098f4 and G17D c3535440...e9cc8251, byte for byte
(check_fwid.py, see below; it reads the firmware files locally and
prints digests and offsets only).

27.0 runs the 26A428 graph. 27.2 and, for now, 27.3 name V26B123_M5,
whose layouts the M5 graph does not build yet, so they are identified
and then refused before any GPU write; 27.3 gets its own variant once
its HW data is built. Probe still refuses the M5 Pro for want of
bare-metal tables. The fwid KUnit tests cover the new builds.

The check scripts are in contrib/validated/aurora/prs/gpu-27.2/checks/
of https://github.com/rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
